 agents.\\" Key changes from v2:\\\\n- Tool Integrity + Injection Exposure + Input Manipulation \xe2\x86\x92 Agent Compromise Indicator\\\\n- Blast Radius absorbed into Agent Action Severity\\\\n- New Resource Consumption Risk dimension (rule-based)\\\\n- All 6 dimensions now pass the server-defense direction test\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'965113b9a8890f2c89f26147054e9fdeb37fd4a5\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-03-30 16:24:13+03:00\\nMessage: \'Emphasize directionality: MCP server is the asset, agents are the threat\\\\n\\\\nMake it unambiguous that the framework defends the server FROM agents,\\\\nnot the other way around. Server is the protected asset; agents are scored\\\\nas potential threats.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'b51373788c471f62e49c6b7c71d595aeab5bdf11\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-03-30 16:11:52+03:00\\nMessage: \'Reframe project description: defense-oriented MCP server protection\\\\n\\\\nClarify that the framework defends MCP servers from malicious/risky agents\\\\n(not general \\"risk modeling\\"). Replace specific CVSS mention with generic\\\\n\\"traditional risk frameworks\\" since many exist.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'389c3a641188ddd9cf99a594231a7de3559524b7\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-03-30 15:35:38+03:00\\nMessage: \'Add v2 agent-boundary dimensions and final datasets report\\\\n\\\\nRefocused 8 ecosystem dimensions into 7 agent-boundary dimensions + 1\\\\nmodifier. Every dimension now answers \\"is THIS call by THIS agent safe\\\\nRIGHT NOW?\\" instead of generic ecosystem risk. Added final report mapping\\\\nall 22 datasets to extractable columns per dimension.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'a0f88541815dca81475b6614b59ceb9d1980a9f1\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-03-30 14:48:42+03:00\\nMessage: \'Add dimension refinement analysis: 11 benchmark dimensions \xe2\x86\x92 8 final MCP-RSS scoring dimensions\\\\n\\\\nData-grounded analysis of all risk dimensions from 22 benchmark files.\\\\nStarts with 18 columns, triages by data support (A/B/C grades),\\\\nmerges 4 overlapping dimensions, and arrives at 8 final dimensions\\\\nwith 1-10 scale specs, row counts, and computation methods.\\\\nReconciles with existing CVSS-inspired thesis metrics.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'50fe629af3275c68924526cc64f923f800f152d2\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-03-30 13:39:20+03:00\\nMessage: \'Add comprehensive README for benchmark_md with skipped list and risk dimensions table\\\\n\\\\nReplaces the basic index with full documentation including:\\\\n- 22 analyzed benchmarks organized by tier (MCP-specific, agent security, scoring frameworks)\\\\n- 52 skipped benchmarks with categorized reasons\\\\n- Unified risk dimensions table mapping 11 dimensions across all benchmarks\\\\n- Practical guide for using the analysis to build a multi-dimensional risk scorer\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'2787908b9651184dd0e2b6dc06575554a9a95135\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-03-30 13:37:33+03:00\\nMessage: \'Add benchmark analyses 13-18: AgentDojo, InjecAgent, Meta PI, ASB, MiniScope, Indirect PI Attack\\\\n\\\\nSix new benchmark analysis files covering prompt injection, permission scope,\\\\nand model vulnerability benchmarks with proposed 1-10 risk dimension mappings.\\\\nUpdated README index with correct metadata for all new entries.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Cl