itereture_review/ -> Literature_review/ to fix misspelling.\\nUpdates all references in standards docs and scripts.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\'\n\nCommit: \'c4c77be06d64410b2883377e4a42b634568487ff\'\nAuthor: <git.Actor "To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>">\nDate: 2026-04-05 11:53:01+03:00\nMessage: \'Consolidate standards docs and remove empty scaffolding\\n\\n- Merge style-guide + naming-conventions into style-and-naming.md\\n- Merge folder-layout + docs-organization into project-layout.md\\n- Delete 3 empty .claude/commands/ files (plan, implement, review)\\n- Delete docs/claude/ files that duplicated CLAUDE.md\\n- Flesh out .gitignore with .env, IDE configs, tool caches\\n- Update all cross-references\\n\\nReduces docs/ from 24 to 19 files (~420 lines removed, ~23%).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\'\n\nCommit: \'4f3346fda11114a12454f8b2a7c467409ca119f3\'\nAuthor: <git.Actor "To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>">\nDate: 2026-04-05 11:31:50+03:00\nMessage: "Add project organization standards: folder layout, naming, data, docs\\n\\nAdds 4 new standards docs + standards README: folder-layout.md,\\nnaming-conventions.md, data-organization.md, docs-organization.md.\\nDerived from Python Packaging Guide, Harvard RDM, and PEP 8 best\\npractices, tailored to this project\'s src/tests/docs/Litereture_review\\nstructure.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n"\n\nCommit: \'78960f80e1c6c572d4200c54be3e9a2e8f0a04cd\'\nAuthor: <git.Actor "To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>">\nDate: 2026-04-05 11:17:28+03:00\nMessage: \'Add clean 6-category server threat taxonomy (38 attacks, CIA-mapped)\\n\\nCondensed server-victim taxonomy organized by attacker goal: Compromise,\\nSteal, Tamper, Bypass, Disrupt, Abuse. Includes Tier 1/2 classification,\\nCVE references, CIA mapping, and Tier 3 excluded-threat table. Sits\\nalongside the detailed mcp_server_attack_taxon