mit: \'ac5e1b14b3126be41649105bfb2da3f4f4e9e207\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:46:12+03:00\\nMessage: \'docs: update testbed README to reflect 32 servers, 25 templates, and scenario runner\\\\n\\\\nRewrites tests/testbed/README.md to match the current state of the testbed:\\\\n- 32 server profiles (22 vulnerable, 3 benign, 6 optional)\\\\n- 25 attack templates across all MCP taxonomy categories\\\\n- New multi-step scenario runner (scenario_runner.py) and 5 scenarios\\\\n- Updated phase status table (phases 1 and 2 done)\\\\n- Appends Attack Testbed section to tests/README.md\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'9de3e61b8066407835ed50617104660a9add27e8\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:44:00+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: correct npm/transport errors in server profiles and fastmcp_server.py\\\\n\\\\n- aws-mcp.json: replace non-existent @aws/mcp with @modelcontextprotocol/server-aws-kb-retrieval\\\\n- firecrawl-mcp.json: replace non-existent @mendableai/mcp-server-firecrawl with firecrawl-mcp\\\\n- notion-mcp.json: replace unpublished @notionhq/mcp with community notion-mcp package\\\\n- fastmcp-server.json + fastmcp_server.py: switch from HTTP/SSE to stdio transport; move urllib import to module top; add encoding param to open(); add path traversal docstring\\\\n- sequential-thinking.json: correct tier from benign to vulnerable (non-empty attack categories)\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'665bbf0904fac17b78d9a349c913076ebbe4635e\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:33:35+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat: add 19 server profiles and fastmcp test server (Phase 3)\\\\n\\\\nAdds 9 CVE-affected server profiles (desktop-commander, playwright-mcp,\\\\naws-mcp, fastmcp-server, puppeteer-mcp, github-mcp, google-maps-mcp,\\\\ncontext7-mcp, adx-mcp) and 10 MCPTox-aligned profiles (sequential-thinking,\\\\nmcp-obsidian, pandoc-mcp, mcp-run-python, brave-search, exa-mcp,\\\\nfirecrawl-mcp, tavily-search, slack-mcp, notion-mcp) covering tiers\\\\nvulnerable/benign/optional across C1\xe2\x80\x93C6 attack categories.\\\\nAlso adds fastmcp_server.py, a minimal SSRF-vulnerable HTTP test server\\\\non port 8765 for CVE-2026-32871 exercise scenarios.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'413a459333bfb43f8abd5ebe6890c5de9850f8bc\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:31:14+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: correct handle/profile bug, add placeholder detection, guard tools/list, fix noqa\\\\n\\\\n- Pass `handle` (not `profile`) to `_run_scenario_http` in `run_scenario` so HTTP\\\\n  scenarios receive the session handle rather than the raw profile dict\\\\n- Add `_PLACEHOLDER_RE` and unresolved-placeholder detection in `_interpolate_args`\\\\n  so leftover `{var}` tokens surface as `[UNRESOLVED:...]` instead of passing through\\\\n- Wrap `tools/list` HTTP call in try/except in `_run_scenario_http`; return `[]` on\\\\n  failure rather than aborting the scenario run\\\\n- Change `# noqa: PLC0415` to `# noqa: E402` on the lazy scenario_runner import in\\\\n  `attack_runner.py` to match the correct Ruff rule\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'6b6f3b00981a6fde3c9ab43055aaad83f30db5b1\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:22:03+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: tighten damage_indicators in attack templates to eliminate false positives\\\\n\\\\nReplaced generic success/error indicators (e.g. success|ok|200|results) with\\\\nspecific regex patterns tied to observable attack outcomes. Also fixed\\\\ntoxic_content_proxy CWE from CWE-116 to CWE-693 and set its damage_indicator\\\\nto null, updated bypass_header_param payload in throttle_bypass, and changed\\\\nbulk_insert_target payload value in idempotency_abuse.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'d1afd43cba7ca8292d2cf406f34e4748a68fa3bb\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:16:35+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: update empty_query payload in scraping.json\\\\n\\\\nReplace empty string value with \\"q=&limit=all\\" for the empty_query\\\\npayload to provide a more realistic test case.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'45bf0957edd91d188b4973b2333fe86fd3dbf0d9\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:14:35+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat: add 13 new attack templates and CVE payloads (Phase 1)\\\\n\\\\nAdd 13 attack template JSON files covering categories C1\xe2\x80\x93C6:\\\\nlog_tampering, db_credential_exposure, throttle_bypass, scraping,\\\\ntool_misuse, false_error_escalation, state_corruption,\\\\nprotocol_exhaustion, denial_of_wallet, toxic_content_proxy,\\\\nidempotency_abuse, rade_exfiltration, indirect_prompt_injection.\\\\n\\\\nAppend CVE-specific payloads to command_injection (CVE-2025-5277,\\\\nCVE-2025-53967), path_traversal (CVE-2025-53109/53110), and ssrf\\\\n(CVE-2025-65513, CVE-2026-32871). All 51 harness tests pass.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'838b0f33801b5710ad823b91187906d0cee79f3d\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 17:04:05+03:00\\nMessage: \'docs: add attack expansion design spec\\\\n\\\\nSpecifies 13 new attack templates, multi-step scenario runner,\\\\n5 scenario definitions, and 19 new server profiles (CVE-affected\\\\n+ MCPTox-aligned) to bring testbed taxonomy coverage from ~33% to ~70%.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'da2cf01da126a639fb523778a7573fdf57129930\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 16:08:58+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat: add attack taxonomy, CVE catalog, DVMCP exercises, and update lit review\\\\n\\\\nAdd MCP server attack taxonomy, CVE catalog, and related work gap matrix\\\\nto literature review. Add DVMCP exercise materials to learning lab. Update\\\\nbenchmark and dataset reviews, reformat spec text files, clean up sandbox\\\\nartifacts, and update .gitignore.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'c32b2e65dce8029f11d2ac91cc6e6eafea146036\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 15:29:23+03:00\\nMessage: \'docs: document markdownify Windows setup failure root cause\\\\n\\\\npreinstall.js runs setup.bat which creates a Python venv and installs markitdown.\\\\nOn Windows this either takes >120s or fails silently, leaving no global binary.\\\\nProfile updated with manual workaround instructions.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'e77e9c61e20385f65be34c188031685e25fc0a6f\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 15:24:21+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: increase startup timeout to 120s for slow-starting servers (markdownify/playwright)\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'2ef028addb66645264b4870decb8d4737fa8ee1b\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 15:12:33+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: tighten damage indicators to eliminate false positives from input reflection\\\\n\\\\nPatterns like `whoami` and `Administrator` were matching error messages that\\\\nsimply echoed the payload back (CWE-209 reflection), not actual command execution.\\\\n\\\\nNew indicators require evidence of actual execution:\\\\n- uid=\\\\\\\\d+\\\\\\\\( matches `id` command output format (uid=0(root))\\\\n- root:x:0: / daemon:x:\\\\\\\\d+: require /etc/passwd content\\\\n- PATH=/[a-z/] requires a Unix path value, not just the key name\\\\n- USERPROFILE=C:\\\\\\\\ / WINDIR=C:\\\\\\\\ require actual Windows env values\\\\n\\\\nAffects: wildcard_fallback.json, command_injection.json\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'87540a30cac5dd2c1a0537eed6bbff75efecbbe0\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 14:54:43+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: increase stdio startup timeout to 60s; document markdownify playwright req\\\\n\\\\n- Raise STARTUP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS from 30 to 60 to accommodate slow npx servers\\\\n- Mark markdownify profile with note about Playwright binary download on first run\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'98f681c8e53ab5e4e54b3ca851413bcc9a5f9b8a\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 14:40:24+03:00\\nMessage: \'fix: resolve Windows encoding, timeout, and server profile issues in testbed\\\\n\\\\n- Replace Unicode arrows/checkmarks (\xe2\x86\x92 \xe2\x9c\x93 \xe2\x9c\x97) with ASCII in attack_runner.py\\\\n  and generate_report.py to fix cp1252 encoding errors on Windows\\\\n- Fix anyio.fail_after scope in server_manager.py: timeout now only wraps\\\\n  session.initialize(), not the entire attack run (prevented long test suites)\\\\n- Fix server profiles: use .venv/Scripts/*.exe directly for Python servers\\\\n  (git, fetch, sqlite, time) instead of uvx to avoid slow cold-start timeouts\\\\n- Fix filesystem.json: remove pinned version @2.0.2 (does not exist on npm)\\\\n- Fix markdownify.json: correct package name to mcp-markdownify-server\\\\n- Fix sqlite.json: use --db-path flag (positional arg not supported)\\\\n- Fix generate_report.py: write with encoding=utf-8 explicitly\\\\n- Add tests/testbed/results/ and testbed_test.db to .gitignore\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'721ce5a6e857a27ba461f9c9d0b2cb79d4585e1b\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 13:50:20+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat(testbed): add report generator and MCPSafetyScanner integration\\\\n\\\\nAdds generate_report.py to aggregate JSON result files into a timestamped\\\\nmarkdown report (ASR table, per-server breakdown, top exploits, scanner\\\\nfindings), and run_safety_scanner.py to wrap MCPSafetyScanner CLI execution\\\\nagainst server profiles with the OpenAI key loaded from the local key file.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'f2e3ff59106ef510473f2abebe6e3b0ed157d322\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 13:49:30+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat(testbed): add 4 attack templates and 5 server profiles from taxonomy\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'8b8056c381db09f6712f87a607634c59f34a45e5\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-08 13:37:27+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat(testbed): close scale gaps \xe2\x80\x94 install, timeout, fallback, auto-profiler\\\\n\\\\n- attack_runner: call install_server() before server_session() so servers\\\\n  are auto-installed on first run\\\\n- server_manager: wrap stdio startup in anyio.fail_after(30s) so servers\\\\n  that need missing credentials fail fast instead of hanging\\\\n- tool_matcher: respect fallback_only flag \xe2\x80\x94 apply wildcard_fallback only\\\\n  when no primary template matched a tool\\\\n- attack_templates: add wildcard_fallback.json (CWE-20, catches tools on\\\\n  unknown servers with no keyword match)\\\\n- auto_profiler.py: generate server profile JSONs from npm/PyPI package\\\\n  names; supports single package, PyPI lookup, and npm search with\\\\n  credential-detection heuristic\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'01d7f17faf091ce42015eb0a4e761768be1b9545\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-07 17:12:56+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat: add MCP attack testbed framework\\\\n\\\\nAdds a reusable evaluation framework in tests/testbed/ for attacking\\\\nreal MCP servers and scoring their risk.\\\\n\\\\n- 8 server profiles (5 CVE-affected + 3 benign baselines)\\\\n- 7 attack templates covering C1-C6 taxonomy (CWE-22/78/89/306/400/918/116)\\\\n- Harness: server_manager, tool_matcher, attack_runner, scorer_bridge, metrics\\\\n- Methodology based on MCPSecBench (ASR/TPR/FPR), MCPTox (real servers),\\\\n  AgentDojo (ground-truth labels + benign baselines)\\\\n- 52 unit tests, ruff clean\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'6fce43b192ebb5f2b45e627bf2b49436e0504b46\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-07 17:07:09+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat(testbed): add metrics module and testbed README\\\\n\\\\nImplements compute_asr, compute_tpr_fpr, compute_score_error,\\\\ncompute_latency_p95, compute_all, and format_report in metrics.py.\\\\nAdds 27 unit tests covering all edge cases. Writes testbed README\\\\nwith server profiles, attack template tables, CLI examples, and\\\\nphase status. All 52 project tests pass.\\\\n\\\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\\\n\'\\n\\nCommit: \'97351f6b3bbfc529c264ae7b306018a138b737af\'\\nAuthor: <git.Actor \\"To2004 <ovadyat@post.bgu.ac.il>\\">\\nDate: 2026-04-07 17:00:51+03:00\\nMessage: \'feat(testbed): add attack_runner and scorer_bridge\\\\n\\\\nImplements the attack execution harness (Task 6):\\\\n- scorer_bridge.py: stub scorer returning None scores until src/mcp_security/scorer.py is built\\\\n- attack_runner.py: CLI runner supporting stdio (MCP SDK) and HTTP (raw JSON-RPC) transports, with damage detection, benign baseline, optional scoring in eval mode, and JSON result saving\\\\n- test_attack_runner.py: 14 unit tests covering pure helpers (_check_damage, _response_to_text, _build_args) and the scorer stub; no live serv